@@ -3,3 +3,13 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` resolves an [RFC 6901 JSON Pointer](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901)
+and returns the selected JSON value. Use the empty string to select the whole document, or a
+slash-prefixed pointer such as `/users/0/name` to select a nested value. Within a reference token,
+`~1` represents `/` and `~0` represents `~`.
+
+It throws for malformed pointers or when a pointer does not select a value in the document. Array
+indices must use canonical non-negative decimal notation (`0` or a number without a leading zero).
